- `resume` (asked, failed): what a new session needs to finish this turn if
  this one is gone: what is done, what is left, local commits or files you
  wrote.
- `next`: what the next turn must check.
- `user`: any decision the user gave you in this terminal during this turn.

If the tool or the command lists problems, fix the record and call again. If
it says {{name}}'s daemon is not running, tell the user and end your turn. The
answer comes as a notice naming its gate: read it with `task_read` or
`'/opt/loop/bin/loop' turn answer https://github.com/acme/api/pull/7`, act on it, then record again.

## Brief

No brief: none is stored for this pull request yet. Guide blocks that need the brief (kind, size, risk, tags, paths) are not in this text.

## Judgment

Parts are in order; where they disagree, the later part wins.

### Your review guide

## Voice

- **Open the body with one line to the author by `@login`**, then the findings.

For anything these instructions do not cover, run `'/opt/loop/bin/loop' help`.
